{"availability":"available","full":"marmelab/react-admin-helpdesk","name":"react-admin-helpdesk","description":"An example react-admin app simulating a help desk UI for support agents","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":65,"forks":21,"created":"2023-01-16T10:53:15Z","updated":"2024-06-21T15:18:13Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://marmelab.com/react-admin-helpdesk","topics":["demo","react","react-admin","reactjs","real-time"],"demo":"https://marmelab.com/react-admin-helpdesk","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:23.658Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:23.658Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:50:23.658Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:25:28.451Z","stars":65,"forks":21},{"at":"2026-10-08T04:50:23.658Z","stars":65,"forks":21}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This application is a fake a Help Desk for an imaginary refrigerator company with a few support agents. You can test it online at It is a demo of the react-admin library.","React-admin usually requires a REST/GraphQL server to provide data. In this demo however, the API is simulated by the browser (using FakeRest). The source data is generated at runtime using Faker.js, so the names and dates change each time you refresh your browser. This demo also simulates real-time activity using an in-memory store (it doesn't work across tabs).","To explore the source code, start with src/App.tsx."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marmelab/react-admin-helpdesk/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2e1d0461600eb56e4214f7ea0d73153b230d3d95960612b3fd446e60ef294cf8","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:28.573Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:28.573Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This application is a fake a Help Desk for an imaginary refrigerator company with a few support agents. You can test it online at It is a demo of the react-admin library.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marmelab/